Venetium 0018 - V8 on Windows ARM32 (thumbv7-pc-windows-msvc).

BATCH-ARM-1 section 3B, his decisions 4 and 7 (ARM-1-DECISIONS.md), drafted against 150's own code (not CR109's). 10 files:
- codegen/arm/constants-arm.h: the "ARM EABI support is required" #error does not apply to _M_ARM (clang-cl's Windows ARM32 target
  does not define __ARM_EABI__, and defining it would be wrong: Windows ARM32 is not the EABI).
- codegen/arm/cpu-arm.cc: FlushICache via FlushInstructionCache(GetCurrentProcess(), start, size) on Windows.
- base/cpu/cpu-arm.cc: Windows ARM32 feature detection with IsProcessorFeaturePresent: NEON (PF 19), VFP 32 D-registers (PF 18),
  integer divide only from PF_ARM_DIVIDE_INSTRUCTION_AVAILABLE (24; Tegra 3 has none), ARMv8 (29).
- base/debug/stack_trace_win.cc: the ARM CONTEXT (Pc/R11/Sp, IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_ARMNT) instead of the IA32 one.
- snapshot/embedded/platform-embedded-file-writer-win.cc: the symbol prefix chosen at run time by the target architecture - no "_" for
  arm (the "_" broke the link: undefined v8_blob), unchanged for the x86 targets, so out/x86-arm-sim keeps working.
- execution/isolate.cc: the embedded blob base is read with bit 0 masked on a Windows ARM host (lld, like link.exe, sets the Thumb bit
  on code-section symbols; the blob is data). Host predicate: isolate.cc also compiles into the x86 mksnapshot.
- heap/base/asm/arm/push_registers_asm.cc: ELF-only .type/.hidden/.size guarded for COFF.
- base/platform/platform-win32.cc: OS::ArmUsingHardFloat() for Windows returns true (Windows ARM32 is hard-float; #error if the
  compiler ever stops defining __ARM_PCS_VFP) - it had no Windows definition (a link error).
- _AddressOfReturnAddress: the three V8 sites (platform-win32.cc, platform.h, utils.cc) take __builtin_frame_address(0) on a
  Windows ARM host: clang-cl defines _MSC_VER, and for thumbv7 that intrinsic is an unresolved external (TOOLCHAIN-ISSUES B2).
  (Moved here from 0022 so every V8 file lives in one patch; Blink's site stays in 0022.)
x86/x64/arm64 objects are unchanged (checked for the x86 snapshot toolchain object by object).

